# code-review-graph index scope — HOME BASE ONLY, optimised as the PROJECT MANAGER map.
#
# Signal = the master toolkit (.agents/ — its scripts, commands, rules, skills, hooks)
# and the routing/docs infrastructure. That toolkit is the whole point: GitNexus could
# never index it (its walker hardcoded `dot: false`, so every dot-directory was skipped
# before ignore rules ran, and the lobby index saw 86 symbols in 18 files). This engine
# indexes whatever `git ls-files` tracks, so .agents/ is in — 1073 nodes on the first
# build — and the job of this file is only to keep the NOISE out.
#
# Why this file and not .gitignore: these paths are tracked on purpose. Ignoring them
# here scopes the graph without changing what git carries.

# ── The sync MIRRORS. Excluding these is the single most important line here. ──
# .agents/ is the master; .claude/, .opencode/, .agent/ and .antigravity/ are generated
# copies of the same commands, skills and hooks. Indexing them re-indexes every toolkit
# symbol three to four times over: measured on the first build, .claude contributed 257
# nodes and .agent 193, all duplicates of .agents/ content.
/.claude/
/.opencode/
/.agent/
/.antigravity/

# Historical session records — append-only walkthroughs, plans and receipts. History,
# not the system: they describe work that is already done and would swamp every query.
/_artifacts/

# The operator's personal notes and brainstorming. Deliberately un-scanned (AGENTS.md §4).
/_my_resources/

# Vendor BMAD install (regenerated, never hand-edited) and its output.
/_bmad/
/_bmad-output/

# Routing test fixtures — deliberately tiny and deliberately weird; graph noise.
/_routing-canary/

# Virtual environments.
/.venv/
/.venv_stale/

# NOTE: Projects/ needs no line. Those are git submodules, so `git ls-files` reports
# them as gitlinks rather than as files, and each carries its own graph. This is the
# trap that forced `.gitnexusignore` to exist: GitNexus walked the filesystem instead
# of the index and swallowed every submodule working tree, ballooning the lobby map to
# ~105k nodes. Verify after any engine upgrade rather than assuming.
